    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d172">

                <pb facs="0441" n="345" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg345"/>

                <head>No. 170.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish to Mr. Williams.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-09-08"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 8,
                        1874</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 184.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my No. 179, I transmit
                    herewith for your information and guidance a copy of a dispatch<anchor n="*"
                        xml:id="d172-f1"/> of July 11, 1874, from J. J. Henderson, esq., our consul
                    at Amoy, transmitting a copy of a proclamation issued by him on the 16th of
                    June, 1874, and correspondence relative to the participation of citizens of the
                    United States in the Japanese expedition to Formosa, and a copy of my reply of
                    the 4th instant, No. 21.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d172-f1" n="*" xml:id="d172-f1-content">
                <p>See correspondence with Mr. Henderson, <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
